# SDR Type 01h - Full Sensor Record used with tests/transcripts/sensor_mask.tr.
#
# The BMC reports a readable-threshold mask of 15h -- the exact complement of
# MaskA's 2Ah: lower non-critical, lower non-recoverable and upper critical are
# readable, the other three are not.  Between the two records every `data[0] &
# bit' guard, and every mask inside the clauses those guards protect, is seen
# both set and clear.
#
# M is 1, B is 0 and both exponents are 0, so every converted threshold equals
# its raw byte and the arithmetic stays out of the way of what these cases are
# for.  Record ID, sensor number and entity use distinct non-zero bytes, per the
# rule in tests/transport/Bmc.zig.

7b e2        # [1:2]  Record ID = 0xe27b
51           # [3]    SDR version 1.5 (51h)
01           # [4]    Record type 01h = Full Sensor Record
30           # [5]    Record length = 48 bytes follow

20           # [6]    Sensor owner ID (BMC)
00           # [7]    Owner LUN 0, channel 0
bb           # [8]    Sensor number BBh
16           # [9]    Entity ID
0e           # [10]   Entity instance
7f           # [11]   Sensor initialization
68           # [12]   Sensor capabilities: thresholds readable+settable
01           # [13]   Sensor type 01h = Temperature
01           # [14]   Event/reading type 01h = threshold
ff 3f        # [15:16] Assertion event mask / lower threshold reading mask
ff 3f        # [17:18] Deassertion event mask / upper threshold reading mask
3f 3f        # [19:20] Settable / readable threshold mask in the *SDR*; the mask
             #        that matters here is the one the BMC returns in byte 0 of
             #        the Get Sensor Thresholds response, not this one.
00           # [21]   Units 1: analog format 0 (unsigned)
01           # [22]   Units 2: base unit 01h = degrees C
00           # [23]   Units 3: no modifier unit
00           # [24]   Linearization: linear
01           # [25]   M = 1 (LS 8 bits)
0d           # [26]   M MS 2 bits = 0, tolerance = 13
00           # [27]   B = 0 (LS 8 bits)
00           # [28]   B MS 2 bits | accuracy LS 6 bits
00           # [29]   Accuracy MS | accuracy exp | sensor direction
00           # [30]   R exponent | B exponent (both 0)
07           # [31]   Analog flags: nominal, normal max and normal min specified
32           # [32]   Nominal reading = 50
5a           # [33]   Normal maximum = 90
14           # [34]   Normal minimum = 20
ff           # [35]   Sensor maximum reading = 255
00           # [36]   Sensor minimum reading = 0
64           # [37]   Upper non-recoverable = 100
5a           # [38]   Upper critical = 90
50           # [39]   Upper non-critical = 80
0a           # [40]   Lower non-recoverable = 10
14           # [41]   Lower critical = 20
1e           # [42]   Lower non-critical = 30
03           # [43]   Positive-going threshold hysteresis
0c           # [44]   Negative-going threshold hysteresis (differs from positive)
00 00        # [45:46] Reserved
00           # [47]   OEM
c5           # [48]   ID string type/length: 8-bit ASCII, 5 characters
4d 61 73 6b 42   # [49:53] "MaskB"
